From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:33:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/33] pinctrl: ingenic: Add X2600 support

The X2600 GPIO and pin controller follows the X2000 one: the same
function, interrupt, pull-up/pull-down, edge and Schmitt trigger
registers, now 0x1000 apart for each of its five ports. Its shadow
registers differ: each port has its own set at +0x800, loaded into the
port by writing 1 to its GLD register at +0x8f0, instead of a shared
port Z loaded by port number.

Add the X2600 with its pin groups, and use per-port shadow registers
for it. Its slew rate register is not documented, so refuse to set or
report the slew rate; the documentation does not say which pins have
pull resistors either, so all are allowed.

The pin groups follow Ingenic's X2600 SDK kernel. A UART with four
pins is described as one group, since the SDK does not say which pin
carries which signal.
